% Test cases for the ankle-foot and knee-ankle-foot orthosis policy
% (afo_kafo.le): synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33686
% and per payment condition of Policy Article A52457, each stating only what
% its record shows. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's,
% the medical reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the
% answer conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first
% query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and
% necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base afo_kafo cases includes these resources:
    afo_kafo.

the knowledge base afo_kafo cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete positioning AFO (L4397) file, the contracture route: a right
% ankle contracture (M24.571) with 15 degrees of dorsiflexion measured with a
% goniometer, the two findings, the stretching program, the diagnosis on the
% claim line, the order and the delivery.
scenario positioning_afo_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the night splint.
    the HCPCS code of the night splint is "L4397".
    the night splint is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "M24.571".
    the dorsiflexion of the ankle of Ann on passive range of motion testing is 15 degrees.
    the passive range of motion of the ankle of Ann was measured with a goniometer before treatment.
    the finding contracture correctable about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding contracture interferes with function about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record documents a stretching program for the ankle of Ann.
    claim 1 states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary.
    the order for the night splint is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the night splint is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the night splint includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the night splint includes order date.
    the order for the night splint includes description of the item.
    the order for the night splint includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the night splint includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the night splint was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the night splint was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the night splint.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Plantar fasciitis (M72.2): criterion 5 alone suffices.
scenario plantar_fasciitis_route is:
    claim 1 is for the night splint.
    the HCPCS code of the night splint is "L4396".
    the night splint is furnished to Ben.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "M72.2".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A fixed contracture: 5 degrees of dorsiflexion on passive range of motion
% testing. Criterion 1 fails.
scenario fixed_contracture is:
    claim 1 is for the night splint.
    the HCPCS code of the night splint is "L4397".
    the night splint is furnished to Cy.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "M24.572".
    the dorsiflexion of the ankle of Cy on passive range of motion testing is 5 degrees.
    the passive range of motion of the ankle of Cy was measured with a goniometer before treatment.
    the finding contracture correctable about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding contracture interferes with function about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record documents a stretching program for the ankle of Cy.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Foot drop (G57.31, lesion of the common peroneal nerve) without an ankle
% contracture: no group 1 diagnosis, not covered.
scenario foot_drop_without_contracture is:
    claim 1 is for the night splint.
    the HCPCS code of the night splint is "L4396".
    the night splint is furnished to Dee.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "G57.31".
    the dorsiflexion of the ankle of Dee on passive range of motion testing is 20 degrees.
    the passive range of motion of the ankle of Dee was measured with a goniometer before treatment.
    the finding contracture correctable about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding contracture interferes with function about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record documents a stretching program for the ankle of Dee.
    rn expects answers [].

% A foot drop splint (L4398): Medicare does not reimburse it.
scenario foot_drop_splint is:
    claim 1 is for the foot drop splint.
    the HCPCS code of the foot drop splint is "L4398".
    the foot drop splint is furnished to Dee.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "M24.571".
    rn expects answers [].

% Replacement interfaces (L4392) for a covered splint: claim 1 comes 90 days
% after the last one, claim 2 seven months after.
scenario replacement_interface_timing is:
    claim 1 is for the early interface.
    the HCPCS code of the early interface is "L4392".
    the early interface is an accessory of the night splint.
    the early interface is furnished to Eve.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    claim 2 is for the later interface.
    the HCPCS code of the later interface is "L4392".
    the later interface is an accessory of the night splint.
    the later interface is furnished to Eve.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-10-15.
    the HCPCS code of the night splint is "L4397".
    the night splint is furnished to Eve.
    the last replacement interface for the night splint was furnished on 2026-03-03.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "M24.575".
    the dorsiflexion of the ankle of Eve on passive range of motion testing is 12 degrees.
    the passive range of motion of the ankle of Eve was measured with a goniometer before treatment.
    the finding contracture correctable about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding contracture interferes with function about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record documents a stretching program for the ankle of Eve.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A complete custom fabricated AFO (L1940) file: an ambulatory beneficiary
% with weakness of the ankle, the findings, the reason for custom
% fabrication, the orthotist's evaluation, the face-to-face encounter and
% the order before delivery (L1940 is on the required list).
scenario custom_afo_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the custom AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the custom AFO is "L1940".
    the custom AFO is furnished to Fay.
    the residence of Fay is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    Fay is ambulatory.
    the medical record of Fay documents weakness of the ankle.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the condition is expected to be permanent".
    the records of the orthotist include a functional evaluation corroborating the need for custom fabrication of the custom AFO.
    the treating practitioner examined Fay for the custom AFO in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the custom AFO is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the custom AFO is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the custom AFO includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the custom AFO includes order date.
    the order for the custom AFO includes description of the item.
    the order for the custom AFO includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the custom AFO includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the custom AFO was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the custom AFO was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the custom AFO.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same AFO for a beneficiary the record does not describe as ambulatory.
scenario nonambulatory_beneficiary is:
    claim 1 is for the custom AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the custom AFO is "L1940".
    the custom AFO is furnished to Gus.
    the medical record of Gus documents weakness of the ankle.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the condition is expected to be permanent".
    rn expects answers [].

% A prefabricated AFO (L1930) with the basic criteria met: no reason for
% custom fabrication is needed.
scenario prefabricated_afo is:
    claim 1 is for the plastic AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the plastic AFO is "L1930".
    the plastic AFO is furnished to Hal.
    Hal is ambulatory.
    the medical record of Hal documents deformity of the foot.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The Council finds the record does not show why a prefabricated AFO would
% not do: the custom fabricated orthosis is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario council_custom_fabrication_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the custom AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the custom AFO is "L1940".
    the custom AFO is furnished to Ida.
    Ida is ambulatory.
    the medical record of Ida documents weakness of the foot.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Ida is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record states only that a custom orthosis was ordered and describes no condition a prefabricated orthosis could not accommodate".
    rn expects answers [].

% A prefabricated KAFO (L2035) with the AFO criteria met and an addition
% (L2210) on it: the knee stability finding is not recorded, so both answers
% are conditional on it.
scenario kafo_knee_stability_open is:
    claim 1 is for the KAFO.
    the HCPCS code of the KAFO is "L2035".
    the KAFO is furnished to Jo.
    claim 2 is for the dorsiflexion assist.
    the HCPCS code of the dorsiflexion assist is "L2210".
    the dorsiflexion assist is an accessory of the KAFO.
    the dorsiflexion assist is furnished to Jo.
    Jo is ambulatory.
    the medical record of Jo documents weakness of the ankle.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding addition medically necessary about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding additional knee stability required about Jo is established"].

% A Charcot restraint orthotic walker (L4631) with a group 2 diagnosis
% (E11.610), and one with a group 1 diagnosis.
scenario crow_diagnosis is:
    claim 1 is for the walker orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the walker orthosis is "L4631".
    the walker orthosis is furnished to Kim.
    claim 2 is for the other walker orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the other walker orthosis is "L4631".
    the other walker orthosis is furnished to Lee.
    Kim is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Kim is "E11.610".
    the medical record of Kim documents deformity of the foot.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "a neurological status requiring custom fabrication to prevent tissue injury".
    Lee is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Lee is "M24.571".
    the medical record of Lee documents deformity of the foot.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Lee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Lee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Lee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "a neurological status requiring custom fabrication to prevent tissue injury".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A torsion mechanism (L2999) assisting knee extension, and one for a
% beneficiary whose record documents a joint contracture.
scenario torsion_mechanism is:
    claim 1 is for the knee extension assist.
    the HCPCS code of the knee extension assist is "L2999".
    the knee extension assist is a concentric adjustable torsion style mechanism assisting knee extension.
    the knee extension assist is furnished to Max.
    the finding joint motion assist required about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the other assist.
    the HCPCS code of the other assist is "L2999".
    the other assist is a concentric adjustable torsion style mechanism assisting knee extension.
    the other assist is furnished to Ned.
    the finding joint motion assist required about Ned is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record of Ned documents joint contracture.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but the orthotist's records hold no functional
% evaluation corroborating the custom fabrication: payable fails at the
% remedy, and the flip names the missing record.
scenario custom_afo_no_orthotist_evaluation is:
    claim 1 is for the custom AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the custom AFO is "L1940".
    the custom AFO is furnished to Fay.
    the residence of Fay is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    Fay is ambulatory.
    the medical record of Fay documents weakness of the ankle.
    the finding stabilization required for medical reasons about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding potential to benefit functionally about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the condition is expected to be permanent".
    the treating practitioner examined Fay for the custom AFO in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the custom AFO is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the custom AFO is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the custom AFO includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the custom AFO includes order date.
    the order for the custom AFO includes description of the item.
    the order for the custom AFO includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the custom AFO includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the custom AFO was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the custom AFO was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the custom AFO.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the records of the orthotist include a functional evaluation corroborating the need for custom fabrication of the custom AFO"]].

